[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4106690277","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117726#issuecomment-4106690277","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117726","id":4106690277,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc70xx7l","user":{"login":"Chaosus","id":3036176,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzYxNzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3036176?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus","html_url":"https://github.com/Chaosus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-22T17:56:30Z","updated_at":"2026-03-22T19:02:10Z","body":"Note: I did not figure out how to update previews when changing parameters via inspector, so I've added \"Update ~uniforms~ parameters\" button at the top of the list - so user may press it when needed. If anybody knows how to get a proper subinspector to connect its \"property_edited\" signal to `ShaderTextEditor` - you're welcome to help.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4106690277/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4106727479","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117726#issuecomment-4106727479","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117726","id":4106727479,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc70x7A3","user":{"login":"cashew-olddew","id":155181921,"node_id":"U_kgDOCT_jYQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/155181921?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cashew-olddew","html_url":"https://github.com/cashew-olddew","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cashew-olddew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cashew-olddew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cashew-olddew/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cashew-olddew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cashew-olddew/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cashew-olddew/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cashew-olddew/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cashew-olddew/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cashew-olddew/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-22T18:19:53Z","updated_at":"2026-03-22T19:17:40Z","body":"I might be misremembering, but when I implemented the addon, I also tried connecting to the `property_edited` signal, but it seemed that the signal was only emitted when an inspector property was modified, but not when the shader parameters were modified.\r\n\r\nThe only way I could achieve a 'live preview' was by tracking and snapshotting the uniform parameters and, in the `_process` function, by updating the preview window only if the params were modified.\r\n\r\nNot sure if this is feasible directly in the engine or if it would affect performance, and most probably you have already noticed the way I did that, but hopefully it helps.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4106727479/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":2},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4106802059","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117726#issuecomment-4106802059","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117726","id":4106802059,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc70yNOL","user":{"login":"Chaosus","id":3036176,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzYxNzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3036176?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus","html_url":"https://github.com/Chaosus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-22T19:07:09Z","updated_at":"2026-03-22T19:07:09Z","body":"> I might be misremembering, but when I implemented the addon, I also tried connecting to the property_edited signal, but it seemed that the signal was only emitted when an inspector property was modified, but not when the shader parameters were modified.\r\n\r\nI've debugged it a bit and seems like `property_edited` should emit when the shader parameter is changed, but it's emitted from a specified subinspector which hidden in the deep of root EditorInspector. I think this is fine to be delayed for improve in further PRs.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4106802059/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4118816816","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117726#issuecomment-4118816816","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117726","id":4118816816,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc71gCgw","user":{"login":"Chaosus","id":3036176,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzYxNzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3036176?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus","html_url":"https://github.com/Chaosus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-24T14:37:34Z","updated_at":"2026-03-24T14:37:34Z","body":"Note: I don't want to overcomplicate this PR, so I've decided to delay adding a menu for breakpoints to future.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4118816816/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4142533706","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117726#issuecomment-4142533706","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117726","id":4142533706,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc726gxK","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-27T13:21:12Z","updated_at":"2026-03-27T14:40:05Z","body":"-  This might be out-of-scope, but is it possible to make the previews work with TEXTURE?\r\n<img width=\"605\" height=\"439\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4a6b43e6-e8f4-4a43-b4c4-e86f632a4e26\" />\r\nThey already require the node to be selected, so I don't see why it shouldn't work.\r\n\r\nEDIT:\r\n- Found some bug:\r\n<img width=\"293\" height=\"374\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6802d2f5-5574-4ece-b536-56dd59176910\" />\r\n\r\nThe last line says I should select the node, but it is already selected (as you can see with other lines).\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>Shader code</summary>\r\n\r\n```\r\nshader_type canvas_item;\r\nrender_mode blend_mix;\r\n\r\nuniform vec2 camera_scene_position;\r\nuniform sampler2D noise_rgb:repeat_enable,filter_nearest;\r\nuniform float power:hint_range(0.01, 1500.0, 0.01) = 10.0;\r\nuniform float sparcle_scale:hint_range(0.1, 10000.0, 0.1) = 100.0;\r\nuniform float motion_scale:hint_range(0.0, 1000.0, 0.001) = 1.0;\r\n\r\n\r\nvarying vec2 global_coordinates;\r\nvoid vertex() {\r\n\tglobal_coordinates = (MODEL_MATRIX * vec4(VERTEX, 1.0, 1.0)).xy;\r\n\t}\r\n\r\nvoid fragment() {\r\n\tvec3 camera_direction = vec3(0.0, 0.70710677, 0.70710677);\r\n\tvec3 random_direction = normalize( texture( noise_rgb, global_coordinates / sparcle_scale).rgb - 0.5 );\r\n\r\n\tfloat value = ( camera_scene_position.x + camera_scene_position.y ) / motion_scale;\r\n\tfloat sin_value = sin(value);\r\n\tfloat cos_value = cos(value);\r\n\t//float sin_value = sin(TIME * 0.5);\r\n\t//float cos_value = cos(TIME * 0.5);\r\n\r\n\r\n\tvec3 view_direction = vec3(1.0, 0.0, 0.0);\r\n\t\r\n\tvec3 rotated = camera_direction;\r\n\trotated.x = camera_direction.x * cos_value - camera_direction.y * sin_value;\r\n\trotated.y = camera_direction.x * sin_value + camera_direction.y * cos_value;\r\n\r\n\tfloat color_influence = 1.0 / max(COLOR.r, 0.0001);\r\n\tfloat sparkle = dot( rotated, random_direction );\r\n\t//float sparkle = dot( camera_direction, random_direction );\r\n\tsparkle = pow( clamp(sparkle, 0.0, 1.0), power * color_influence );\r\n\r\n\tCOLOR.rgb += COLOR.rgb*vec3(sparkle);\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\nEDIT2:\r\nAnother case:\r\n<img width=\"548\" height=\"295\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ec624a43-2a3a-46be-9c7f-a0429b449ab7\" />\r\nLooks like this can randomly happen on some lines?\r\n\r\n- The whole editor jumps when a scrollbar appears.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/97ca066e-f913-408a-95eb-1f1b0600756e\r\n\r\nYou can use SCROLL_MODE_RESERVE to alleviate that (although it adds an unused margin if the scrollbar is invisible).\r\n\r\n- It could be useful to allow closing the previews without a need to click the breakpoint. E.g. with a X button somewhere.\r\n\r\n- 3D previews take too long to initialize.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c0fd9ae6-fee6-4951-9938-47b583ad2a69\r\n\r\nThe editor freezes for a few seconds when you put a breakpoint. It will probably be better in official builds, but some optimization would be nice anyway.\r\n\r\n- The previews are gone once shader is closed. Shouldn't they get saved, like script breakpoints?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4142533706/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4142809268","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117726#issuecomment-4142809268","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117726","id":4142809268,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc727kC0","user":{"login":"cashew-olddew","id":155181921,"node_id":"U_kgDOCT_jYQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/155181921?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cashew-olddew","html_url":"https://github.com/cashew-olddew","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cashew-olddew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cashew-olddew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cashew-olddew/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cashew-olddew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cashew-olddew/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cashew-olddew/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cashew-olddew/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cashew-olddew/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cashew-olddew/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-27T13:57:53Z","updated_at":"2026-03-27T14:17:26Z","body":">They already require the node to be selected, so I don't see why it shouldn't work.\r\n\r\nThe original addon updates the texture of the TextureRect defining the preview window to that of the currently selected node. Maybe it could work here as well.\r\n\r\n> The last line says I should select the node, but it is already selected (as you can see with other lines).\r\n\r\nIn your example:\r\n```gdshader\r\n...\r\nfloat sparkle = dot( rotated, random_direction );\r\n//float sparkle = dot( camera_direction, random_direction );\r\nsparkle = pow( clamp(sparkle, 0.0, 1.0), power * color_influence );\r\n...\r\n```\r\nThere is a comment right after the `sparkle` variable definition. I noticed that the `_find_statement` function forgets to strip comments. \r\n```CPP\r\nif (start < p_line && (current_line.is_empty() || current_line.ends_with(\";\") || current_line.ends_with(\"{\") || current_line.ends_with(\"}\"))) {\r\n\t\t\treturn false;\r\n}\r\n```\r\nCould it be that the code finds the \";\" inside the comment and fails to parse correctly?\r\n\r\nI noticed that other functions like `_find_var_type` do this check:\r\n```CPP\r\nString TextShaderPreview::_find_var_type(const PackedStringArray &p_lines, const String &p_var_name, int p_line) {\r\n...\r\n\tfor (int i = p_line; i >= 0; i--) {\r\n\t\t// Strip out comments before checking so we don't catch commented-out declarations.\r\n\t\tString clean_line = p_lines[i].split(\"//\")[0];\r\n\r\n\t\tRef<RegExMatch> m = type_regex->search(clean_line);\r\n\t\tif (m.is_valid()) {\r\n\t\t\treturn m->get_string(1);\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t}\r\n...\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4142809268/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4143144177","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117726#issuecomment-4143144177","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117726","id":4143144177,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7281zx","user":{"login":"Chaosus","id":3036176,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzYxNzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3036176?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus","html_url":"https://github.com/Chaosus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-27T14:46:34Z","updated_at":"2026-03-27T16:27:03Z","body":"> node to be selected, so I don't see why it shouldn't work. \r\n\r\nIts possible, but `MaterialEditor` used in preview use `ColorRect` rather than `TextureRect` which doesn't have a texture property. Changing it may break the canvas_item previews and overcomplicate the code. I think this may be delayed for other PR.\r\n\r\n> 3D previews take too long to initialize.\r\n\r\nOn screencast, you've initialized multiple previews. Currently, every preview in a single shader file regenerates every time the \"breakpoint_toggled\" signal emitted. I know that's not optimal, but It's too hard for me at the moment to figure out how to do it without bugs where user removes and pushes lines between or before breakpoints, so I did it like that.\r\n\r\n> The previews are gone once shader is closed. Shouldn't they get saved, like script breakpoints?\r\n\r\nSame, I think this could be delayed for fix in future PRs. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4143144177/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4143374665","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117726#issuecomment-4143374665","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117726","id":4143374665,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc729uFJ","user":{"login":"Chaosus","id":3036176,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzYxNzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3036176?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus","html_url":"https://github.com/Chaosus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-27T15:20:36Z","updated_at":"2026-03-27T15:20:49Z","body":"> The whole editor jumps when a scrollbar appears.\r\n\r\n> It could be useful to allow closing the previews without a need to click the breakpoint. E.g. with a X button somewhere.\r\n\r\nFixed\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>Details</summary>\r\n\r\n<img width=\"744\" height=\"1164\" alt=\"изображение\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c11bf9e9-10ad-4106-ba6b-8d96199c6efc\" />\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4143374665/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4155330246","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117726#issuecomment-4155330246","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117726","id":4155330246,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc73rU7G","user":{"login":"Qubus0","id":51323316,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMzIzMzE2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51323316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Qubus0","html_url":"https://github.com/Qubus0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Qubus0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Qubus0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Qubus0/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Qubus0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Qubus0/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Qubus0/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Qubus0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Qubus0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Qubus0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-30T14:07:06Z","updated_at":"2026-03-30T14:07:06Z","body":"> The editor freezes for a few seconds when you put a breakpoint. It will probably be better in official builds, but some optimization would be nice anyway.\r\n\r\nwouldn't this also require threaded shader compilation? since all of the shaders are re-compiled completely every time, leading to even larger editor hangs. so unless that is implemented (if ever) there isn't much to optimize apart from trying recompile the least amount of shaders possible. \r\nmaybe adding refresh buttons to each of them, but that seems like a big ux loss as well. but maybe more bearable than double the waiting time when changing a large shader, also considering manual shader reload has already been proposed to reduce hanging during editing https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12352","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4155330246/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4161748200","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117726#issuecomment-4161748200","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117726","id":4161748200,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc74Dzzo","user":{"login":"Chaosus","id":3036176,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzYxNzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3036176?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus","html_url":"https://github.com/Chaosus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-31T10:55:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-31T10:55:27Z","body":"> The breakpoint_color should be changed at least (to white probably).\r\n\r\nDone\r\n\r\n> The previews are not saved when closing and reopening the shader, they probably should be.\r\n\r\nAs I said I don't want to overcomplicate this PR - this could be implemented later.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4161748200/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4176277305","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117726#issuecomment-4176277305","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117726","id":4176277305,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc747O85","user":{"login":"QbieShay","id":7917475,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MTc0NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7917475?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay","html_url":"https://github.com/QbieShay","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-02T10:37:12Z","updated_at":"2026-04-02T10:37:12Z","body":"I may be too \"old school everyone must suffer as I did\" to fully appreciate this feature, but I think this is great.\r\n\r\nHow does this work with shader include files? Does it work? Does it show an error? Do you think it's possible to support also visually debugging included files? (not for this PR if it's hard)\r\n\r\nIn my personal wishlist I think I'd add a color picker that tells me the raw value of the pixel :D but again not necessary for this PR (it also may turn a bit complicated to do due to color space conversions)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4176277305/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":1,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4176609974","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117726#issuecomment-4176609974","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117726","id":4176609974,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc748gK2","user":{"login":"Chaosus","id":3036176,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzYxNzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3036176?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus","html_url":"https://github.com/Chaosus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-02T11:10:16Z","updated_at":"2026-04-02T11:12:02Z","body":"> How does this work with shader include files? Does it work? Does it show an error?\r\n\r\nNeither of this - user just cannot set up these breakpoints in shader include files. Its only allowed in common shaders.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4176609974/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4178979100","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117726#issuecomment-4178979100","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117726","id":4178979100,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc75Fikc","user":{"login":"blueskythlikesclouds","id":19259897,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjU5ODk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19259897?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds","html_url":"https://github.com/blueskythlikesclouds","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-02T16:19:20Z","updated_at":"2026-04-02T16:20:16Z","body":"Just spitballing here but do you need to compile a shader for every breakpoint? I would've imagined something like a software breakpoint:\r\n\r\n```glsl\r\nvec3 v = texture(tex, UV).rgb;\r\nvec2 v2 = vec2(sin(v.x), cos(v.y));\r\nvec3 v3 = vec3(0, 0.25, 0.5);\r\nvec2 v4 = UV;\r\n```\r\n\r\ncompiles to:\r\n\r\n```glsl\r\nvec3 v = texture(tex, UV).rgb;\r\nif (BREAKPOINT_LINE == 6) {\r\n    COLOR = vec4(v, 1.0);\r\n    return;\r\n}\r\nvec2 v2 = vec2(sin(v.x), cos(v.y));\r\nif (BREAKPOINT_LINE == 7) {\r\n    COLOR = vec2(v, 0.0, 1.0);\r\n    return;\r\n}\r\nvec3 v3 = vec3(0, 0.25, 0.5);\r\nif (BREAKPOINT_LINE == 8) {\r\n    COLOR = vec2(v3, 1.0);\r\n    return;\r\n}\r\nvec2 v4 = UV;\r\nif (BREAKPOINT_LINE == 9) {\r\n    COLOR = vec2(v4, 0.0, 1.0);\r\n    return;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThen you can reuse this shader for every breakpoint and set the BREAKPOINT_LINE uniform to get the result of the line you want.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4178979100/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4182471905","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117726#issuecomment-4182471905","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117726","id":4182471905,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc75S3Th","user":{"login":"cashew-olddew","id":155181921,"node_id":"U_kgDOCT_jYQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/155181921?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cashew-olddew","html_url":"https://github.com/cashew-olddew","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cashew-olddew/followers","followi