l if the lines were highlighted when you hover over the points, and the preview drew an outline around itself, since with a large number of lines it's difficult to tell which line leads where.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4229574950/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4275331086","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117726#issuecomment-4275331086","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117726","id":4275331086,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7-1GAO","user":{"login":"vaner-org","id":9658355,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2NTgzNTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9658355?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org","html_url":"https://github.com/vaner-org","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-19T06:20:56Z","updated_at":"2026-04-19T06:56:27Z","body":"This is a transformative upgrade, great work and great to see it merged.\r\n\r\nIf what I'm about to share doesn't interfere with planned follow-ups, I think this could be improved even more by:\r\n- Making some of the info/buttons smaller and contextual rather than persistent, like the toggle itself. These would be placed specifically to avoid overlapping with the preview controls inside the square, and the toggle to the right.\r\n- Replacing the very spartan line with maybe a transluscent alternating highlight polygon that bridges both sides, although its legibility will obviously be inferior to what we have now. The highlight could be strongest for the careted line if in code or hovered preview if its line is visible, resolving @JekSun97's suggestion.\r\n\r\nObviously there's a lot more to consider in such a compact design than my suggestion can, and there's never a need to compromise on current functionality, but I wanted to offer my thoughts.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"832\" height=\"590\" alt=\"inline-shaders\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1201794e-82f7-478e-adee-a997c7c97575\" />\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4275331086/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]